{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["If he is a hireling — who hired his fellow's animal to do his work with it." "He comes with his hire — that is, he gives him hire, and he is not like a borrower; therefore he is exempt for unavoidable loss, but for theft and loss he is liable like a paid bailee. And there are those who say that even for theft and loss he is exempt and is liable only for negligence, like an unpaid bailee — the dispute of R. Meir and R. Yehudah in Bava Kamma."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:42:35.484318651Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}